Done. Wrote `ros2_stack/docs/mcu_protocol_spec.md` (165 lines), covering everything requested:

- **§1–2 Wire framing** — `A5 | total_len | {sub_len type mod payload}+ | sum&0xFF | 5A`, multi-subpacket batching (BATTERY+VERSION+MOTORS, BMS_VERSION+mod7 at 1 Hz), exact parser/validation contract from `mcu_frame_decode.py` (`inner[0] == len(inner)-2`, checksum over `total_len..payload`), 4096 B ring buffer.
- **§3 Escaping** — `F5 01/02/03` for `A5/5A/F5`, applied to everything between SOF and EOF both directions, including the checksum.
- **§4–5 Types & module ids** — TypeID 0 (host→MCU) / 8 (MCU→host) / 255 (heartbeat), plus OTA-only ids 21/22/37/23/16 flagged as bootloader-path; full ModuleID table (3 charge, 4 speed, 5 battery, 9 imu, 10 sensor, 11 cutter, 12 version, 13 motors, 18 calib, 19 log, 24 bms_version, plus observed-but-undocumented mod 7 = +600/s uptime tick `?`).
- **§6–7 Payload structs** — both directions with sizes, live-calibrated units (voltage 0.1 V), and `(?)` markers on current/MotorInfo units, cutter speed scale (1000 seen), height_motor garbage.
- **§11 Heartbeat/failsafe** — known: 8-byte wall-clock payload, `DevHealthHandler::{updateHeartbeat,checkHeartbeat}`, MCU-side estop/lift/bumper cut-offs; unknown: period, timeout, failsafe behavior (must characterize on hardware).
- **§9 /odom + /cmd_vel + PID** — cmd_vel → `SpeedData{linear m/s, angular rad/s}`; MCU takes linear/angular only; host-side wheel PID (`libpid_controller.so`); odometry host-computed from SpeedData + JY61P yaw at 100 Hz.
- **§10 Topic list with rates** — measured 100/33/3.3/1.7/1 Hz rates, pub/sub/service inventory, and the 60 Hz→33 Hz sensor decimation.
- **§12 Driver checklist** — 16 items from serial bring-up through safety validation.

Two source discrepancies are preserved rather than papered over: MOTORS rate (README ~1 Hz vs header ~2 Hz, written as 1–2 Hz) and the MOTORS/BMS batching detail. Source dirs were untouched; only the one spec file was written.
